{title: The LORD Looks at the Heart}
{subtitle: 1 Samuel 16:7–13; 17:40–50; 16:23; 2 Samuel 11:2–4; 12:7; Psalms 51:3–14}
{key: G}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [G] | [G] | [C] |
| [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Out on the hills [G]by Bethlehem a [C]ruddy shepherd boy
[D]Kept his father's flock by night and sang [C]his songs of [G]joy
Seven brothers passed the prophet, [C]tall and fine to see
But [D]the LORD looks at the heart, and [C]the youngest one was [G]he
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Down in the Valley of Elah a [C]giant cursed and roared
[D]The soldiers stood there trembling, ev[C]ery hand upon [G]a sword
A boy ran out with just a sling, [C]a stone and nothing more
And [D]the giant fell before him, for [C]the battle belongs to [G]the LORD
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G/B]Shep[C]herd boy and gi-[G]ant-sla-yer, [D]harp-play-er and [G]king
A [C]heart that ran to [G]God in ev[D]ery song he'd sing
He [C]fell and he got up [G]again, [D]he wept and he [Em]believed
The [C]LORD looks at the heart, and [D]a broken heart's re[G]ceived
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Up on a palace rooftop in the [C]evening's fading light
A [D]king took what was not his and hid [C]it out of [G]sight
Then Nathan stood before him and [C]said, You are the man
And [D]David fell before the LORD and wept [C]with empty [G]hands
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Have [Em]mercy on me, O [C]God
Wash me, [D]and I will be whiter than snow
Cre[Em]ate in me a clean heart, O [C]God
Renew a [D]steadfast spirit within me
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Shep[C]herd boy and gi-[G]ant-sla-yer, [D]harp-play-er and [G]king
A [C]heart that ran to [G]God in ev[D]ery song he'd sing
He fell [C]and he got up again, [G]he wept [D]and he believed
The [Em]LORD looks at the [C]heart, and a broken heart's re[D]ceived
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The LORD looks at [G]the heart
{end_of_verse}

